      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Doorstep Delivery Handover, Inventory Verification &amp; Placement at Sunkadkatte</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Upon arrival at the Sunkadkatte site, the delivery team initiates a daylight verification process to confirm that every item matches the original inventory bilty.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The team conducts a visual inspection under natural light, checking model numbers, serial tags, and condition markings.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Any discrepancies are logged immediately, photographed, and reported to the logistics coordinator before the uncrating begins.</span></li></ul>

<p>Once verification is complete, the uncrating phase proceeds with a systematic testing regimen for all electrical and mechanical components. Power tools, lighting fixtures, and HVAC units are plugged into a dedicated test circuit, while mechanical assemblies such as door operators and lift mechanisms are cycled through their full range of motion.</p>
<p>Results are recorded on a standardized checklist; items that fail functional tests are isolated for warranty claim processing.</p>

<p>After successful testing, the clean‑room crew positions each piece of furniture according to the floor‑plan schematic. Surfaces are wiped with a low‑lint, anti‑static cloth, and protective films are removed only after placement to avoid scratches. The layout is double‑checked against the design drawing to ensure correct orientation, spacing, and accessibility.</p>

